      "englishText": "Niṣiddhākṣarī:\t(to the Avadhānī) Please give one more syllable\n\nAvadhānī: 'rtya', (thus creating the word 'martya' meaning mortal)\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: 'va' is prohibited (anticipating the word 'vapu' meaning body)\n\nAvadhānī: 'lo'\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: (anticipating the word 'loka' meaning the world) 'ka' is forbidden.\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 2nd time)\n\nAvadhānī: 'nge' (skillfully completes the first pāda or quarter with the syllable 'nge'. Thus the first quarter of the verse reads as follows:\n\namartyātmāmartyalo'nge\n(An immortal soul in a mortal body)\n(The completion of the first pāda is confirmed by the President. The next item is Samasya. Here the last quarter of a śloka is given by a questioner in the form of a riddle. The Avadhānī has to compose the first three lines and complete the śloka, solving the riddle while remaining faithful to the poetical metre.)",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "नष्िाधाक्षरी अन्यः एकः अक्षरः दीयताम्\n\nअवधानी: र्त्य\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी: व वकारः निषिद्धः\n\nअवधानी: लो\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी: ङ्गे ङ्गेकारः निषिद्धः\n🔔 (घण्टा २द्ध\n\nअवधानी: ङ्गे\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी: एकः पादः परिसमाप्तः ।\n\nअवधानी: अनन्तरं समस्या:",
