      "englishText": "(Now it is the turn of the Varṇanā questioner.)\n\nVarṇanā: In this assembly we find a variegated audience, — there are the lovers of Sanskrit, there are the questioners, and there are all those who are in same way devoted and working for Sanskrit. Please compose a poem in Mālinī metre on this topic.\n\nAvadhānī: Do you want me to describe this assembly?\n\nVarṇanā: Yes, right.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: Should he compose in Malini6, or in Manini7? I believe, he knows the ways of Manini well.\n\nAvadhānī: No, Māninī is not necessary. I already have a Māninī (meaning his wife at home).\n\nVarṇanā: Since the respected Avadhānī has  come to this place (alone), so she has become a Māninī8.\n\nCommentator: That means she is angry.\n(The Avadhānī completes then the first quarter of the Varṇanā-item):\n\nThe Bell: (sounds here for the 5th time)\n\nAvadhānī: mahitavividhabhDshDsatkriyDbhushitangDh\n\n(The honoured who are assembled here speak different languages;\ntrue conduct are their ornaments)\n\nPresident: (sums up): The Avadhānī was asked by the questioners to compose a verse in Mālinī metre, describing this assembly. Here he has completed the first quarter.\n\n6A metre of fifteen syllables.\n 7'Manini' means woman. Metre in Sanskrit is called 'vritta' which also means 'the way'. \n 8Here Manini is used in the sense of a dejected lady.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "वर्णना: अत्र सभायां विविधप्रकारकाः सामाजिकाः समसेवकांश्च पृच्छकाः सन्ित । एतानध्िावत्य, सभामध्िावत्य मालिनीवृत्तो किमपि पद्यम् ।\n\nअवधानी: सभास्थानम् ?\n\nवर्णना: आम् सभास्थानम् ।\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः: किं भोः मालिनी वा मानिनी वा ? एते तु मानिनीवृत्तं सम्यव् जानन्ित ।\n\nअवधानी: मानिनी नावश्यकी । एका मानिनी अिस्त मम ।\n\nवर्णना: अवधानी:महाशयः अत्र आगतः इति सा मानिनी जाता\n\nव्याख्याकारः: कुपिता जाता इत्यथ्र्ाः 🔔 (घण्टा ५द्ध\n\nअवधानी: महितविविधभाषासत्क्रियाभूषिताङ्गाः\n\nसभापतिः: वर्णने मालिनीवृत्तो इयं सभा व.र्ानीया इति पृच्छकैः पृष्टम् । तत्र अवधानिना प्रथमः पादः उक्तः । महितविविधभाषासत्क्रियाभूषिताङ्गाः ।",
