      "englishText": "Vyastākṣarī: The tenth syllable is 'gad'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'gad'.\n\nVyastākṣarī: Sir the second syllable is 'ra'.\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the14th time)\n\nCommentator: One question came to my mind while sitting here, in this assembly. Shall I ask? You (the Avadhānī) told the audience that you are a bird and for that you used the word 'vihangamikD', which is in feminine gender. Now I have a doubt, whether you are a man or a woman.\n\nAvadhānī: Who I am truly will be known at the end of this programme. But let me tell you, that you are also feminine in nature. I am of feminine nature, as well as she, as well as he over there. For everyone is in reality   (a woman) Prakriti.\n\nPresident:\t(explains) The whole world consists of these two (principles) — masculine and feminine: The Lord alone is the Supreme Person, the Supreme Man. Everything else, around Him — is of feminine Nature.17\n\nVyastākṣarī: Sir, the fourteenth syllable is 'va'.\n\n17The reference here is made to the ancient Sankhya philosophy, who envisioned one Supreme Being and Conscious Principle, Purusha, while all else, the outer world, is a creation of Prakriti, which exists yet for His Pleasure. The reference is also to the symbolism of Sri Krishna's play with the Gopis as propounded in the Vaishnava system; where Krishna is the only Purusha, while all human beings are souls as Gopis aspiring for Krishna.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "व्यस्ताक्षरी: दशममक्षरं गद्*\n\nअवधानी: दशममक्षरं गद्*\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी: आर्य द्वितीयमक्षरं रा* 🔔 (घण्टा 14)\n\nव्याख्याकारः: सभ्येऽिस्मन् मम एकः प्रश्नः\nवर्तते । अपि पृच्छामि ?\nअहं काचन विहमिका इत्युक्तं मम संशयः जातः भवान् पुमान् वा श्री वा ?\n\nअवधानी: वस्तुतः कः इति सभान्ते निणर्ेतल्यम् । भवती अपि श्री । अहमपि श्री । सापि श्री । एषा सवर्ापि प्रवतिरेव ।\n\nसभापतिः: श्रीप्रायमितरं जगत् । भगवतः समाधौ भगवान् एवैव परमपुरुषः । भगवतः समाधौ अन्यत् सर्वम् श्रीप्रायः ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी: आर्य चतुर्दशमक्षरं व*",
