      "englishText": "(The 3rd and 4th round of Avadhāna)\n\n(Here, as there was a shortage of time the President asked the Avadhānī to complete the 3rd and 4th pādas of all the incomplete stanzas.):\n\t\nAvadhānī: (Avadhānī composes the third and fourth pāda of the Niṣiddhākṣarī-śloka)    \n\nkritye kushalatDbrahma\nrupitam yena te namah\n\n(To Thee, who hast established the Brahman of perfection in works, to Thee my obeisance)\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 15th time.)\n\nPresident: Herewith the task given by the Niṣiddhākṣarī is completed.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: To whom is the obeisance given?\n\nAvadhānī: To him who is behind us\n\n(pointing to Sri Aurobindo's photo)\n\nVyastākṣarī: The third syllable is 'va'.\n\nAvadhānī. 'va'\n\nPresident: Now the third pāda of the Samasyā should be composed.\n\nThe Bell: ( sounds for the 16th time)\n\nAvadhānī: kanthe'pyakanthe virahe priyD me\n\n(and he adds to it the fourth line which \nhad been originally given by the \nSamasyā-questioner)\n\nbhagnDpyabhagnD mama pushpamDlD\n\n(It is around my neck and yet it is'nt, \nin the absence of the beloved ,\nIt is broken, and yet it is \nunbroken, my garland \nof flowers!)",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "निषिद्धाक्षर्याः तृतीय-चतुर्थपादौ\n\nअवधानी: वत्ये--- (घण्टा 15द्ध\nकुशलता ब्रह्म (सभापतिः:- तृतीयः पदः पू.र्ाःद्ध :पितं येन ते नमः\n\nसभापतिः: निषिद्धाक्षरी: श्लोकः सम्पू.र्ाः ।\n\nअपस्तुतप्रसः कस्मै अयं नमस्कारः ?\n\nअवधानी: यः पृष्ठतः अिस्त\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी: तृतीयमक्षरं व*\n\nअवधानी: तृतीयमक्षरं व*\n\nसभापतिः: समस्या:यां तृतीयः पादः (घण्टा 16द्ध\n\nअवधानी: क.ठेऽप्यक.ठे विरहे प्रिया मे\nक.ठेऽप्यक.ठे विरहे प्रिया मे\nभग्नाप्यभग्ना मम पुष्पमाला ।",
