      "englishText": "President: The Samasyā has been completed. Now the third and fourth line of the Dattapadī-item is to be composed.\n \nAvadhānī: nutDnavishkrtikDrini surucirD divyajjaganmangalD\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 17th time).\n\nAvadhānī: pratnD te shubhamurtiradya hridaye dhDryD    vrishDdrishvara \n(Discoverer of new things, beautiful, \nheavenly, ancient, auspicious on earth, \nis Thy shining image. May we hold it today \nin our  heart chamber, O Vrishadrishvara !)\n\nPresident: The four quarters of the Dattapadī-item are herewith completed. Now the third and fourth pāda of the Varṇanā are to be taken up.\n\nVyastākṣarī: The twelfth syllable is 'ksha'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'ksha'.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: Revered Avadhānī, in your\n\nverse you have worshipped Lord VrishDdrishvara, \nor was it Goddess VrishDdrishvari (his female counterpart). Is Lord SrinivDsa masculine or feminine for you?\n\nAvadhānī: He is BDlDji18.  \n\nPresident: If the concluding two lines of the Varṇanā are composed, then it will be complete.\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 18th time)\n\nAvadhānī: atulitabalavidyDdharmarakshaikadiksDh\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 19th time).\n\n(continues) iha sadasi sadasyDh panditDh me'tibhDgyDt//\n(Unequalled in power and knowledge, dedicated to the protection of Dharma, the scholars of this assembly (are present here) due to my good fortune.)\n\nNow the last Eshu?\n\n18In Hindi 'ji' is added at the end of a name as a sign of respect. 'Balaji' is another name of Lord Srinivasa of Tirupati. The Avadhānī splits the word Balaji into 'bala' and 'ji'. 'Bala' in Sanskrit is feminine meaning a girl. Thus the Avadhānī has solved the problem elegantly, with a pun and play of words.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "सभापतिः: समस्या: सम्पूणर्ा । पुनः दत्तपद्याम् तृतीयः चतुर्थः ।\n\nअवधानी: नूत्नाविष्वतिकारिणी--- (घण्टा 17द्ध नूत्नाविष्वतिकारिणी सुरुचिरा दिव्यज्जगन्मङ्गला\nप्रत्ना ते शुभमुहूर्तोऽद्य हृदये धायर्ा वृषाद्रीश्वर ।\n\nसभापतिः: दत्तपद्याम् पादचतुष्टयं सम्पूर्णम् । सम्प्रति वर्णने पादद्वयम् । तृतीयः पादः चतुर्थः पादः ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी: द्वादशमक्षरं क्ष*\n\nअवधानी: द्वादशमक्षरं क्ष*\n\nअपंस्तुतप्रसः भोः अवधानिवर्य! वृषाद्रीश्वरं स्तुतवान् वा वृषाद्रीश्वर! स्तुतवान् वा ?\nश्रीनिवासं कां कां वा मन्यते भवान् ?\n\nअवधानी: सा बालाजी\n\nसभापतिः: वर्णने पादद्वयं दीयते तर्हि अवधानम् सम्पूर्णं भविष्यति । 🔔 (घण्टा 18)\n\nअवधानी: अतुलितबलविद्याधर्मरक्षैकदीक्षाः (घण्टा 19द्ध\nइह सदसि सदस्याः पण्डिताः मेऽतिभाग्यात् ।\n\nअन्ितमः आशुः ?",
